compromise of several hundred Israel-made and U.S.-made fuel management systems in Israel and the United States."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1190"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Hide IOCONTROL in payment terminal"],["description","IOCONTROL was hiding inside Gasboy's Payment Terminal, called . An attacker with full control over the payment terminal means they had the ability to shut down fuel services and potentially steal credit card information from customers."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1543.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Resolve C2 via DNS over HTTPS"],["description","First, the malware uses Cloudflare\u2019s servers to translate the hostname into an IP address. In order to evade detection, the malware does not use DNS to translate this hostname directly, instead it uses to translate it via CloudFlare\u2019s API. This is a stealth technique used by malware to avoid being detected by sending a clear-text DNS request, showcasing which DNS names they communicate with. Instead, they used an encrypted protocol (HTTPS), meaning that even if a network tap exists, the traffic is encrypted so they won\u2019t be discovered."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1071.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Install boot script backdoor"],["description","Before connecting to the C2 infrastructure, the malware first installs a backdoor on the device in order to ensure its persistence. To do so, the malware adds a new boot script, which will be executed whenever the device restarts. The backdoor is located in , contains the following bash script:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1037.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Store malware binary as /usr/bin/iocontrol"],["description","In addition to this backdoor, the malware is stored under the name in the directory."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1574.007"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Connect to MQTT C2"],["description","After translating this hostname into IP address, the malware takes the second configuration parameter: 8883, and uses it as the port to connect to the C2. Port 8883 is usually used by the\u00a0 MQTTs communication protocol, and when examining the code further we indeed saw that the malware indeed communicates over this port."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1071.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Publish MQTT hello message"],["description","After connecting to the MQTT broker, the malware immediately publishes an \u201c \u201d message to the following topic: . This message informs the C2 of a new connection, and sends a lot of identification information about the infected device."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1071.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Execute OS commands for device profiling"],["description","In order to get this information (for example, the current user, hostname etc), the malware uses OS commands. In this process, the malware gets a handle to the library by calling with the parameter . Then, using this handle, the malware gets the pointer to the system function using , giving it the function name , and lastly uses this pointer to execute the OS commands it needs."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Subscribe to MQTT push topic"],["description","After sending the message, the malware subscribes to the MQTT topic {GUID}/push. Using this topic, the C2 sends the malware commands for execution, which the malware executes inside the callback routine that is called whenever a MQTT message is received."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1071.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c"